What does this function compute?
function calc(n):
  if n == 0: return 1
  return n * calc(n-1)

What does this do?
function foo(arr, n):
  for i = 0 to n-2:
    for j = 0 to n-i-2:
      if arr[j] > arr[j+1]:
        swap(arr[j], arr[j+1])

What does the following pseudo code return for n=4?
function mystery(n):
  if n <= 1: return n
  return mystery(n-1) + mystery(n-2)
